                <pb facs="0605" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-07-02T15:00:00-04:00">July 2, 1948—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>973. NAC agencies including ECA by unanimous informal vote today agreed to
                    previous NAC recommendation re Article VII (new Article V) para 5 (Embtel 1149
                    June 25 <hi rendition="#italic">et seq</hi>.) with following amendment
                    interpolated between “The Government of China” and “shall hold the remaining
                    balance”: “in agreement with the Government of the United States”. Emb should
                    therefore substitute NAC language transmitted Deptel 900 June 19 including this
                    amendment (Note Dept comment Deptel 920 June 24). Dept anticipates no Chinese
                    objection new language this section.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
